---
description: Keep service classes thin; avoid helper-method sprawl
globs: app/Service/**/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# Service Helper Methods

- Do not split one small concern into multiple private methods in a service class.
- Prefer keeping simple orchestration inline in `create`, `updateById`, or other public methods.
- When logic is reusable or non-trivial, move it to the appropriate existing layer instead of adding service helpers:
  - formatting/normalization → `App\Support\*`
  - persistence checks/queries → repository
- One problem should not become three private methods unless each method is reused in multiple public entry points.
